        "id": 211295031,
        "iid": 8792,
        "project_id": 34675721,
        "title": "stack: import an existing stack from a merge request",
        "description": "### Problem\n\n`glab stack` keeps its metadata only in the local `.git/stacked/`.\nA stack created on another machine, or by a teammate, cannot be worked with locally.\n`glab stack infer` builds a new stack from commits, but creates new branches, so `glab stack sync` would open duplicate merge requests.\n\n### Proposal\n\n`glab stack import <mr>` rebuilds the local stack metadata from GitLab:\n\n1. From the given MR, follow `target_branch` down to the base branch, and follow MRs whose `target_branch` is the current `source_branch` up to the top.\n2. Write one `StackRef` per MR (`prev`, `next`, `branch`, `mr`, `description`) plus `BASE_BRANCH`. For glab-named branches (`<prefix>-<title>-<sha>`), title and SHA come from the branch name; otherwise from flags or generated.\n3. Create local branches tracking the remote ones and set the stack as current.\n\nAfterwards `glab stack sync` updates the existing MRs instead of creating new ones.\n\n### Open questions\n\n- Several open MRs targeting the same branch: refuse or prompt?\n- Support MRs from forks in the first version?\n\nWriting these files by hand for an existing 5-MR stack worked: `glab stack list` showed it correctly.",
