        "id": 211171533,
        "iid": 8790,
        "project_id": 34675721,
        "title": "mr create --wip should behave the same as of mr create --draft",
        "description": "### Problem to solve\n\nWhen passing `--wip` to `mr create`, the resulting MR title will be prefixed with `WIP:`, which as far as I know is not very useful, as it has no special meaning to Gitlab, so I don't see any use case for `--wip`.\n\n### Proposal\n\nPassing `--wip` to `mr create` should prefix the MR title with `Draft:` instead of `WIP:`, as Draft has a meaning for Gitlab.\n\nThis mean that `--wip` should not be \"an alternative\" to `--draft`, instead, an alias.\n\nAnother possibility is to simply remove the `--wip` option completely to prevent confusion. Manually adding a `WIP:` to the MR title is simple enough not to need any special handling within the tool.\n\n### Further details",
        "state": "opened",
